{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$U = V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to W$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-locally-finite-type-fppf-local-source}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:17fb76800a009679de67dc3124a4c5e67e39018b7087a0c958bb2f48569f46cf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4c4e7998369da0394fecc69cb5613c6c7cff86ed5fa68229cca7d91e92633668", "source_text": "Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002>. Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0003> and a surjective smooth\nmorphism <MATH_0004>. Set\n<MATH_0005> which is an algebraic space.\nWe know that <MATH_0006> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation\nand that <MATH_0007> is locally of finite type.\nHence the lemma reduces to the case of morphisms of algebraic spaces.\nThe case of morphisms of algebraic spaces is\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b8753c325c555e8eb96077cead539d65775d1b3cd318c28a5dc22f3d26d417a", "unit_id": "tag:06U8:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$g : \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$g \\circ f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-type-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ac4353a855249546103888725355403c0062042fc9043effa2b591462e58503", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:418b0dddfd9e9226d887831097cf8893c7357bd84d57f675502480d526d5b23b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002> be morphisms of algebraic stacks.\nIf <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type,\nthen <MATH_0004> is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:941c5e6c33dea08a144d51e3fc741bc91f8818b1fe865fad0dec983c0b125a42", "unit_id": "tag:06U9:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nU \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & V \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & W \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Z}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$W$", "MATH_0005": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} W$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} V$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} V$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\to W$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-permanence-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d239fc33ee9cd600ccd696677e36ad4e304133903c93134c8c44b1e9d149e0b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a33061b24428de1799f6fe777c71617e57e2c877266be31364009bcd905c0ea2", "source_text": "We can find a diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nwhere <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> are schemes, the vertical arrow <MATH_0005>\nis surjective and smooth, the arrow <MATH_0006>\nis surjective and smooth, and the arrow\n<MATH_0007> is surjective and smooth.\nThen also <MATH_0008> is surjective and\nsmooth (as a composition of a surjective and smooth morphism with a\nbase change of such). By definition we see that <MATH_0009> is locally\nof finite type. Hence <MATH_0010> is locally of finite type by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwhich in turn means (by definition) that <MATH_0011>\nis locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe3919e41a5d9a277319b7852a1e3af9a8a4974ee42188abcd900b886bdd3ebd", "unit_id": "tag:06U9:proof"}
